# Per-product landing page overrides

## Goal
Let a product ship a custom landing page (distinct `<main>` sections) without
giving up the shared data-driven `/docs` subroutes or hand-writing a document
shell. Products without a custom landing keep the current generic hero+CTA
automatically.

## Approach: component-slot convention via `import.meta.glob`
- Override components live at `src/components/product-landing/<slug>.astro`,
  one per product, keyed by filename = product `slug`.
- A small resolver (`src/lib/product-landing.ts`) eagerly globs that directory
  at build time and returns the component for a given slug (or `undefined`).
- Both landing routes (`src/pages/[product]/index.astro` and its
  `src/pages/[locale]/[product]/index.astro` twin) call the resolver; if an
  override exists they render it, otherwise they render the extracted shared
  fallback `src/components/ProductLandingDefault.astro`.
- The override renders **only the `<main>` sections** (hero, custom sections,
  CTA). The route continues to own `Layout` + `Nav` + `Footer` and the `<head>`
  (title / description / alternates / locale) — matching the existing
  `DocsLayout` pattern and the `agents.md` rule against a second document shell.
- Docs subroutes (`/<product>/docs`, `/<product>/docs/[...slug]`) are
  **untouched**: they remain data-driven off the `products` array.

## Contract for an override component
Props (identical for the fallback and every override, so they are interchangeable):
- `product: Product` — full entry from `src/config/products.ts` (slug, name,
  github, badges, base, nav).
- `locale: Locale` — current locale (`'en'` from the default route, the loop
  variable from the `[locale]` twin).
- `c: ProductCopy` — locale-resolved UI strings (`c.viewSource`,
  `c.documentation`, `c.ctaTitle`, …), so overrides reuse shared labels.
- `docsHref: string` — base-aware, locale-prefixed docs link, pre-computed by
  the route so the override does not re-derive `withBase`/`localizePath`.

The override returns `<section>` blocks only (no `<main>`, no `Layout`).
To localize custom copy, the override may branch on `locale` internally; v1
ships **one override per product, used across all locales**. Per-locale override
files are a future extension (noted in `agents.md`, not built now).

## Files

### New
1. `src/lib/product-landing.ts` — glob resolver.
   - `import.meta.glob('../components/product-landing/*.astro', { eager: true })`.
   - Parse slug from each key's filename, build a `Record<string, Component>`.
   - Export `getProductLanding(slug): Component | undefined`.
   - Export `ProductLandingProps` type (`{ product, locale, c, docsHref }`)
     and `ProductLandingComponent` type so overrides/fallback share one shape.

2. `src/components/ProductLandingDefault.astro` — the current generic hero +
   CTA, extracted verbatim from the two twin routes. Accepts the same props as
   an override. Shared by both routes as the fallback.

3. `src/components/product-landing/vite.astro` — worked example override:
   custom hero lead + a small feature grid, reusing `c` / `docsHref` for
   actions and existing CSS classes (`.product-hero`, `.section`, `.btn`,
   `.container`) plus one scoped `.feature-grid` block. Demonstrates the
   contract for future products.

### Edited
4. `src/pages/[product]/index.astro` — import resolver + `ProductLandingDefault`;
   compute `const Override = getProductLanding(product.slug)`; replace the
   inlined `<main>` hero+CTA with a single
   `{Override ? <Override .../> : <ProductLandingDefault .../>}` branch.
   `Layout` / `Nav` / `Footer` / `alternates` / `getStaticPaths` unchanged.

5. `src/pages/[locale]/[product]/index.astro` — identical change (twin). The
   `getStaticPaths` `locales` loop is unchanged.

6. `agents.md` — under **Pages & routing**, document the override convention
   (location, contract, automatic fallback) and add
   `src/components/product-landing/` to the directory-layout note.

## De-risking notes
- **Typing the resolved component.** Primary: `import type { Component } from 'astro'`.
  If `astro check` rejects that import, fall back to a structural type
  `(props: ProductLandingProps) => unknown`. `npm run build` catches this
  either way; it is a typing detail, not an architectural risk.
- **Glob scope.** The glob scans only `src/components/product-landing/*.astro`,
  so `ProductLandingDefault.astro` (flat in `src/components/`) can never be
  picked up as an override.
- **`getStaticPaths` unchanged.** Every product still gets a landing page;
  override resolution happens at render time, not path-generation time.

## Verification
1. `npm run build` — must pass `astro check` + build with no errors.
2. Inspect rendered HTML to confirm override-vs-default behavior:
   - `dist/vite/index.html` — contains the custom feature grid from
     `product-landing/vite.astro`.
   - `dist/astro/index.html` and `dist/json-server/index.html` — contain the
     generic hero/CTA from `ProductLandingDefault.astro`.
   - `dist/zh-Hans/vite/index.html` — confirms the override renders in the
     `[locale]` twin too.
3. Summarize what changed, what to review, and the override convention for
   future products.

## Out of scope (future extensions, noted in `agents.md` only)
- Per-locale override files (e.g. `vite.zh-Hans.astro`).
- Optional `title` / `description` fields on `Product` for custom `<head>`
  meta (the route currently derives title from `product.name` + `productCopy`).
